\newlabel{fig:opm_setup}{{5.1}{40}{Schematic layout of a radio-frequency OPM. The alkali vapor is spin-polarized along the static field ($B_{\mathrm {DC}}$) by a $\sigma ^+$ pump beam. An orthogonal AC magnetic field excites the Larmor precession, which rotates the polarization plane of a perpendicular, linearly polarized probe beam. This optical rotation is detected by a polarimeter and analyzed using a lock-in amplifier. Adapted from \cite {deans2021}}{figure.caption.54}{}}
